course: dictionary
lesson: 13620
title: Hard to digest, hard to read
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from smaller parts. Indigestible has three: «in-» means not, «digest» means to break food down in your stomach, and «-ible» means able to be. So indigestible means not able to be broken down.
explain: Use the context to check. «The tough skin of the bean was indigestible, so it passed through the body whole.» The skin was not broken down, so indigestible must mean hard or impossible for the stomach to break down.
explain: The word can also describe ideas and books. «The dense, dull textbook was indigestible for Sam, so he gave up reading it.» Dense and dull are clues that the book was hard to understand.
fact: Indigestible means hard or impossible for the body to break down.
fact: «Indigestible» is built from «in-» (not) and «digestible» (able to be digested).
fact: Fibre is mostly indigestible, but it is good for you because it helps your digestive system work well.
fact: «Indigestible» can also mean hard to understand or accept, like a heavy, boring textbook.
fact: The opposite of indigestible is digestible, which means easy for the body to break down.
exercise: «The tough skin of the bean was indigestible.» What does indigestible mean here? | *Too hard for the stomach to break down | Tasty and easy to chew | Full of sugar | Cold and wet
exercise: Which word means the opposite of indigestible? | *Digestible | Impossible | Tough | Hungry
exercise: «The textbook was indigestible for Sam, so he gave up.» What does indigestible suggest here? | Very tasty | Full of pictures | Easy to read in one go | *Hard to understand
test: Fibre is mostly indigestible, so why is it still good for you? | *It helps your digestive system work well | It turns into muscle | It gives you energy straight away like sugar | It makes food taste sweeter
test: Which word is built from «in-» (not) and «digestible»? | Ingredient | Digestible | *Indigestible | Digestive
exam: Explain in your own words why fibre can be indigestible and still be good for you. | It gives you more energy than sugar | It is the same as meat | *It moves through the gut and helps digestion | It is turned into muscle
